{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/145297-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-comics-manga-graphic-novels","id":145297,"title":"Favorite World of Darkness-Esque Comics/Manga/Graphic novels","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-21T21:51:47-07:00","id":145297,"title":"Favorite World of Darkness-Esque Comics/Manga/Graphic novels","content":"Borrowing from rderekp, i was thinking on the penn and papper media. not just books but comics and such..which ones are your favorites or that you could recomend?<br /> Manga: Monster<br /> <br /> Graphic Novels: From Hell, The Crow , The Crow Curare, 30 Days by Night, Lovecraft, Lock and Key, Hellboy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T22:59:33-07:00","id":145332,"title":"","content":"Can't go wrong with Hellsing. Except for the name of the primary character. &quot;Alucard,&quot; sigh. Oh well, still a damn good series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T12:32:57-07:00","id":145920,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strangeways_%28comics%29\" target=\"_blank\">Strangeways: Murder Moon</a> (Werewolf: the Wild West)<br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strangeways_%28comics%29\" target=\"_blank\">High Moon</a> (Werewolf: the Wild West)<br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pride_of_Baghdad\" target=\"_blank\">Pride of Baghdad</a> (W:tA, involving Simba)<br /> <a href=\"http://www.barnesandnoble.com/listing/2682032589739?r=1&amp;cm_mmc=GooglePLA-_-Book_5To14-_-Q000000633-_-2682032589739\" target=\"_blank\">First Moon</a> (Not so WOD-ish according to W:tA, but is about Roanoke and Croatoan.)<br /> <br /> <u>Semi-Graphic Novels:</u><br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Sandman:_The_Dream_Hunters\" target=\"_blank\">Sandman: The Dreamhunters</a> (Was referenced in W:tA books at the time it came out, about a Kitsune.)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/473784993/resurrectionist\" target=\"_blank\">Resurrectionist </a><br /> <br /> <u>Manga:</u><br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ginga:_Nagareboshi_Gin\" target=\"_blank\">Ginga: Nagareboshi Gin</a> (W:tA, only three volumes of the Weed series was translated.)<br /> <a href=\"http://www.animenewsnetwork.com/encyclopedia/manga.php?id=2795\" target=\"_blank\">Half Wild</a> (W:tA, hasn't been translated. And it's for one certain scene that happens in the manga. I managed to pick up a whole set of this manga when I visited Little Tokyo.)<br /> <br /> Also, Moonstone put out graphic novels based on V:tM and W:tA.<br /> <a href=\"http://atopfourthwall.blogspot.com/search/label/Longbox%20of%20the%20Damned\" target=\"_blank\">And Linkara recommends certain horror comics when he does Longbox of the Damned for October. </a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","user":"Laughing Hyena","date":". 05-22-2014, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T13:02:24-07:00","id":145943,"title":"","content":"Tsukihime, Kara No Kyoukai and Decoration Disconnection Disorder can evoke personal horror vibe.<br /> <br /> Mind you, Tsukihime is pretty old visual novel with awkward h-scenes, but when it's serious it's pretty atmospheric. Especially in one route where the MC is slowly losing mind and going batshit insane.<br /> <br /> Kara No Kyoukai is a novel, but I advise to watch movie series. The fan translation of one guy called Cokesakto is, ironically, quasi Mage: The Ascension fanfic with lots of liberties taken regarding the canon. The concept of Counter Force is similar in some way to Paradox, but not exactly the same.<br /> <br /> DDD is about people with mental derangements getting creepy powers and being referred as Possessed. Kinda similar in Fomori, but there are no really demonic entitites behind that. True Demons are apparently discussed in untranslated volume 2, and are something different.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 05-22-2014, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T22:03:09-07:00","id":146369,"title":"","content":"Only fairly recently got into Grant Morrison's <i>The Invisibles.</i> It definitely shares some thematic DNA with Mage: the Ascension.<br /> <br /> Similarly, primary villains The Four in Warren Ellis' <i>Planetary</i> have a good deal in common with the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T22:44:06-07:00","id":146409,"title":"","content":"<br /> For Mage<br /> The Invisibles by Grant Morrison Vertigo<br /> Sex Criminals from Image (paiging Cult of Ecstasy)<br /> Day of Judgment<br /> <br /> Fables is a great example of how baddass Changelings, also check out A Wolf Among us video game based on the comics. again Vertigo<br /> Neil Gaimen's Sandman and the Books of Magic both great for Mage and Changeling.<br /> <br /> Watchmen, ignore the superheroics and check out the world it takes place in. the dirty grimmy New York streets dimly lit by crass neon lights while monsters (Rorschrach) with their own ideas of morality hid in the deepening shadows...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2708-lost_in_the_hedge777","name":"Lost_in_the_Hedge777","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T23:12:52-07:00","id":146443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laughing Hyena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/145297-favorite-world-of-darkness-esque-comics-manga-graphic-novels?p=145920#post145920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Manga:</u><br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ginga:_Nagareboshi_Gin\" target=\"_blank\">Ginga: Nagareboshi Gin</a> (W:tA, only three volumes of the Weed series was translated.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Omg, you know Ginga! Yay ^^<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/membe